WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.893 --> 00:00:13.900
The next time Dr.

2
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:17.423
Warren visited Pollyanna, he was accompanied by another doctor.

3
00:00:20.285 --> 00:00:21.105
"Dr. Chilton!

4
00:00:21.586 --> 00:00:23.527
I'm so glad to see you!"

5
00:00:24.068 --> 00:00:27.610
Pollyanna shouted happily before she remembered her aunt's opinion of him.

6
00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:34.475
"Oh, but if Aunt Polly doesn't want you—" "It's all right, my dear."

7
00:00:35.436 --> 00:00:38.097
Aunt Polly put down the book she'd been reading to Pollyanna.

8
00:00:38.117 --> 00:00:39.939
"I told Dr.

9
00:00:39.979 --> 00:00:41.660
Warren that I wanted Dr.

10
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.061
Chilton to examine you."

11
00:00:44.642 --> 00:00:46.503
"Oh, you asked him to come."

12
00:00:47.664 --> 00:00:50.706
Pollyanna smiled contentedly at this explanation.

13
00:00:50.726 --> 00:00:53.367
"Yes, dear, I asked him.

14
00:00:54.088 --> 00:00:59.371
That is Seeing the adoring look on Dr.

15
00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:04.293
Chilton's face, Aunt Polly turned red, sprang from her chair, and ran from the room.

16
00:01:06.554 --> 00:01:08.914
Dr. Chilton followed Aunt Polly with his eyes.

17
00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:17.597
"Well, Pollyanna He cleared his throat, but his voice was still shaking with emotion.

18
00:01:17.617 --> 00:01:22.438
"Well, Pollyanna, you've just done the gladdest thing of all!"

19
00:01:22.458 --> 00:01:24.679
"I have?"

20
00:01:25.779 --> 00:01:27.980
Pollyanna didn't understand what was going on.

21
00:01:29.596 --> 00:01:32.097
"Yes, you've done something to make me very glad.

22
00:01:33.298 --> 00:01:35.159
Now let's take a look at those legs."

23
00:01:39.241 --> 00:01:42.302
At the end of the day, Aunt Polly returned to Pollyanna's bedside.

24
00:01:42.322 --> 00:01:46.404
"Oh, Aunt Polly, you look so pretty!"

25
00:01:46.744 --> 00:01:47.564
Pollyanna said.

26
00:01:47.584 --> 00:01:51.846
"You look like you did when I dressed you up with the rose and shawl.

27
00:01:52.327 --> 00:01:53.147
What has happened?"

28
00:01:56.388 --> 00:02:00.469
Aunt Polly laughed, a joyous laugh that Pollyanna had never heard before.

29
00:02:00.489 --> 00:02:04.771
"I want you to be the first person to know—Dr.

30
00:02:04.851 --> 00:02:08.392
Chilton is going to be your uncle Thomas!

31
00:02:09.692 --> 00:02:10.932
We're getting married!

32
00:02:13.153 --> 00:02:15.954
We're both so happy, and it's all thanks to you."

33
00:02:15.974 --> 00:02:20.175
"Oh, Aunt Polly, that's wonderful news!"

34
00:02:21.475 --> 00:02:24.476
Pollyanna started to clap her hands but stopped.

35
00:02:25.804 --> 00:02:26.525
"Wait a minute.

36
00:02:27.385 --> 00:02:32.309
Does that mean you were the woman whose hand and heart he wanted a long time ago?"

37
00:02:33.871 --> 00:02:34.771
Aunt Polly nodded.

38
00:02:34.791 --> 00:02:41.517
"We broke off our engagement after a silly argument, but you brought us together again."

39
00:02:43.258 --> 00:02:45.280
Pollyanna suddenly understood.

40
00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.762
"So that's why Dr.

41
00:02:47.822 --> 00:02:50.424
Chilton said I'd done the gladdest thing of all.

42
00:02:51.745 --> 00:02:55.308
I'm so glad right now that I don't even mind about my legs!"

43
00:02:57.688 --> 00:03:03.673
"Someday you might Aunt Polly didn't dare to raise Pollyanna's hopes that she might walk again.

44
00:03:05.675 --> 00:03:07.857
She smoothed Pollyanna's hair with her hand.

45
00:03:07.877 --> 00:03:13.942
"Next week you're going on a long trip to stay with a great doctor.

46
00:03:14.982 --> 00:03:16.223
He's a friend of Dr.

47
00:03:16.283 --> 00:03:20.167
Chilton's, and he runs a clinic just for patients like you.

48
00:03:21.368 --> 00:03:23.770
We're going to see if there's anything he can do for you."

49
00:03:25.531 --> 00:03:28.169
"Oh, Aunt Polly, if he's a friend of Dr.

50
00:03:28.209 --> 00:03:30.451
Chilton's, I'm sure he can help me."

51
00:03:38.436 --> 00:03:43.120
Many months later Aunt Polly and Uncle Thomas received a letter that made them very glad.

52
00:03:44.821 --> 00:03:48.764
Dear Aunt Polly and Uncle Thomas, I can walk!

53
00:03:50.485 --> 00:03:54.248
Today I walked all the way from my bed to the window!

54
00:03:55.592 --> 00:03:59.835
It was only six steps, but oh, how good it felt to walk again.

55
00:04:02.116 --> 00:04:04.657
All the doctors stood around and smiled.

56
00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:09.620
A lady who walked for the first time last week stood at my door and watched.

57
00:04:10.961 --> 00:04:15.784
Another lady, who hopes to walk next month, lay on the other bed in my room and clapped

58
00:04:15.824 --> 00:04:16.404
her hands.

59
00:04:17.665 --> 00:04:22.168
It was like a party except both ladies and all the nurses were crying.

60
00:04:23.836 --> 00:04:26.378
I don't understand why everybody was in tears.

61
00:04:27.739 --> 00:04:30.441
I wanted to sing and shout and bang doors!

62
00:04:32.582 --> 00:04:37.045
After walking today, I don't mind that I've been here almost ten months.

63
00:04:38.246 --> 00:04:43.690
You made sure that I didn't miss the most important event that happened during that time: your wedding!

64
00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:49.213
I still can't believe you got married right here at my bedside!

65
00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:55.469
Not only did I get to attend your wedding, but so did all the doctors and nurses and

66
00:04:55.529 --> 00:04:56.570
patients and staff.

67
00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:01.392
Your wedding made everybody at the clinic feel glad!

68
00:05:02.992 --> 00:05:05.473
The doctors say I'll soon be going home.

69
00:05:05.493 --> 00:05:08.875
I wish I could walk all the way there.

70
00:05:08.895 --> 00:05:14.177
I don't think I'll ever want to ride anywhere again.

71
00:05:14.197 --> 00:05:19.039
(Well, maybe I'll want an occasional ride in your carriage, Uncle Thomas.

72
00:05:19.499 --> 00:05:21.120
I always loved that!)

73
00:05:22.908 --> 00:05:26.469
Oh, I'm so glad about everything these days.

74
00:05:27.509 --> 00:05:30.790
I'm even glad that I lost the use of my legs for a while.

75
00:05:31.911 --> 00:05:36.212
You never realize how lovely legs are until you don't have them.

76
00:05:36.232 --> 00:05:39.653
(I mean, legs that work, of course!)

77
00:05:41.113 --> 00:05:43.554
I'm going to walk eight steps tomorrow!

78
00:05:44.975 --> 00:05:49.516
With lots of love to everyone in Beldingsville, Pollyanna
